What Your Day Will Look Like: 
 We have a great opportunity for an outstanding individual to join the Consor team as an Intern . Under the supervision of our transportation planning team, the intern will engage in a variety of project tasks including data analysis, community outreach, GIS analysis and map making, and developing written reports. The intern receives instructions and technical guidance on specific assignment objectives, methods, and possible solutions. Assistance is provided by Consor staff, and work is reviewed for application of planning principles and best practices in multimodal transportation planning. The position is part-time (approximately 20 hours, which can be negotiated) with the potential to become a full-time internship in the summer. An internship with Consor is classified as temporary but may lead to full-time employment.
 Pay Range: $20–$25/hour
 What You'll Do: 
 Support the Consor Denver office transportation planning team on a range of projects including safety studies, corridor plans, grant applications, curbside planning, and active transportation plans;
 Conduct geospatial analysis and develop map-based visualizations;
 Make or revise maps, charts, exhibits and diagrams;
 Prepare exhibits for community outreach events;
 Attend and facilitate community outreach events;
 Prepare community surveys and synthesize survey results;
 Utilize Microsoft Office Suite programs to analyze data, develop presentations, and support development of reports;
